WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.209
<v Examiner>Karyotypes and aneuploidy.

2
00:00:03.209 --> 00:00:03.970
<v Examiner>Four marks.

3
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.803
<v Examiner>What is a human karyotype, and how many chromosomes does it show?

4
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:10.084
<v Examiner>What is aneuploidy?

5
00:00:10.084 --> 00:00:13.657
<v Examiner>Give two examples, and explain how aneuploidy arises.

6
00:00:14.107 --> 00:00:16.866
The hook: forty-six is twenty-three pairs.

7
00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:19.757
One too many, or one too few, is aneuploidy,

8
00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:23.238
and it comes from a pair failing to split in meiosis.

9
00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:28.372
A karyotype is a picture of a cell's chromosomes, taken at metaphase,

10
00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:32.446
arranged into numbered homologous pairs, by decreasing size.

11
00:00:32.446 --> 00:00:34.483
It's the complete diploid set.

12
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:39.341
Humans have forty-six chromosomes, which is twenty-three pairs:

13
00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:43.750
twenty-two pairs of autosomes, and one pair of sex chromosomes.

14
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.919
X X in a female, X Y in a male.

15
00:00:46.369 --> 00:00:50.097
Aneuploidy is an abnormal number of chromosomes in a cell.

16
00:00:50.097 --> 00:00:51.447
Too many, or too few.

17
00:00:52.897 --> 00:00:53.799
Two examples.

18
00:00:53.799 --> 00:00:59.493
Down syndrome, which is trisomy twenty-one: three copies of chromosome twenty-one,

19
00:00:59.493 --> 00:01:01.367
so forty-seven chromosomes.

20
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:04.631
And Turner syndrome: only one X, so forty-five.

21
00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.894
Edwards syndrome, trisomy eighteen, is another.

22
00:01:08.344 --> 00:01:10.488
How it arises: non-disjunction.

23
00:01:10.488 --> 00:01:16.228
A pair of chromosomes, or its chromatids, fails to separate in anaphase of meiosis,

24
00:01:16.228 --> 00:01:16.989
one or two.

25
00:01:16.989 --> 00:01:23.213
So a gamete gets one chromosome too many, or one too few, and so does the zygote it makes.

26
00:01:24.663 --> 00:01:25.358
The traps.

27
00:01:25.358 --> 00:01:30.572
Forty-six chromosomes is twenty-three pairs: twenty-two pairs of autosomes,

28
00:01:30.572 --> 00:01:32.866
plus one pair of sex chromosomes.

29
00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:35.229
"Twenty-three autosomes" is wrong.

30
00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:38.704
Second: Turner is forty-five, Down is forty-seven.

31
00:01:38.704 --> 00:01:43.501
Third: non-disjunction happens in meiosis, when the gametes are made.

32
00:01:43.951 --> 00:01:44.608
<v Examiner>Once more.

33
00:01:44.608 --> 00:01:46.319
<v Examiner>Karyotypes and aneuploidy.

34
00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:53.968
A karyotype is a picture of the chromosomes in numbered homologous pairs:

35
00:01:53.968 --> 00:02:00.308
forty-six chromosomes, twenty-three pairs, twenty-two pairs of autosomes plus X X or X Y.

36
00:02:00.308 --> 00:02:03.727
Aneuploidy is an abnormal number of chromosomes.

37
00:02:03.727 --> 00:02:08.072
Down syndrome is trisomy twenty-one, forty-seven chromosomes.

38
00:02:08.072 --> 00:02:11.420
Turner syndrome is forty-five, with only one X.

39
00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:16.263
It arises from non-disjunction in meiosis: a pair fails to separate,

40
00:02:16.263 --> 00:02:19.540
so a gamete gets one too many, or one too few.
